# NRA-IDE Cursor Bootstrap Rules
# FILE: .cursorrules / 2026-06-27 17:12 JST

Before starting any task or action, read:

1. `AGENTS.md` — common authority and permission kernel

Then follow the conditional read gates defined in `AGENTS.md`.

Do not read `CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`, or `CLINE.md` merely because Cursor is the host IDE.
Read an adapter file only when the active agent is the matching agent and its own runtime requires it.

This file grants no additional permission.
